# Dolphin GameCube pad seed (-> ~/.config/dolphin-emu/GCPadNew.ini); Dolphin's own default is
# keyboard-only, i.e. a dead controller. Face buttons follow the letters on the RP6's buttons,
# which are Nintendo-style (A east, B south, X north, Y west), not the GameCube's positions.
# The pad reports buttons by position, with xpad's lettering: the west button sends code 0x133
# and the north one 0x134, which evdev names NORTH and WEST. So the north button (X) is "WEST"
# here and the west one (Y) "NORTH" (the same order as the button:2/button:3 indices in Eden's
# seed).
# Z is R1; the analog L and R triggers are L2 and R2, as on the GameCube.
# The trailing " 0" belongs to the evdev device name — drop it and Dolphin binds nothing.
# Dolphin's evdev backend numbers axes in event-code order: on that pad X Y Z RX RY RZ HAT0X
# HAT0Y are Axis 0-7. It has no "Hat" inputs, so the d-pad is Axis 6/7. The triggers rest at
# their minimum, and "Axis 2+" only covers the top half of travel; "Full Axis" spans all of it.
[GCPad1]
Device = evdev/0/Microsoft X-Box 360 pad 0
Buttons/A = EAST
Buttons/B = SOUTH
Buttons/X = WEST
Buttons/Y = NORTH
Buttons/Z = TR
Buttons/Start = START
Main Stick/Up = `Axis 1-`
Main Stick/Down = `Axis 1+`
Main Stick/Left = `Axis 0-`
Main Stick/Right = `Axis 0+`
C-Stick/Up = `Axis 4-`
C-Stick/Down = `Axis 4+`
C-Stick/Left = `Axis 3-`
C-Stick/Right = `Axis 3+`
Triggers/L = `Full Axis 2+`
Triggers/R = `Full Axis 5+`
Triggers/L-Analog = `Full Axis 2+`
Triggers/R-Analog = `Full Axis 5+`
D-Pad/Up = `Axis 7-`
D-Pad/Down = `Axis 7+`
D-Pad/Left = `Axis 6-`
D-Pad/Right = `Axis 6+`
Rumble/Motor = Strong
